.yarn/build-state.yml
.yarn/install-state.gz
.pnp.*
app/build
lib/bundle
pages-dist

.claude
__pycache__/

# Figure bytes live in s3://jbrowse.org/msaview-figures/ and git tracks
# media.lock instead. `pnpm media:pull` installs them; scripts/media-store/
# README.md says why. The nine below stay tracked because the root README and the
# lib, cli and python package READMEs link them by relative path,
# which GitHub resolves against the repo and npm rewrites to a raw URL: dropping
# them breaks those images with no build to catch it, and a store URL carries a
# content hash that would go stale on the next regen. They are also the figures
# nobody regenerates.
docs/media/*
!docs/media/cli-clustalx.png
!docs/media/cli-domains.png
!docs/media/cli-letters.png
!docs/media/cli-quickstart.png
!docs/media/example-domains.svg
!docs/media/example-protein.svg
!docs/media/python-entropy-and-clicks.png
!docs/media/python-quickstart.png
!docs/media/r-quickstart.svg
